<title>SINGAPORE: Flextech plans S$21 mln R&amp;D centre.</title>
<headline>Flextech plans S$21 mln R&amp;D centre.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Electronics and industrial distributor Flextech Holdings said on Thursday it would spend Singapore $21 million on a research and development programme.</p>
<p>It said in a statement the programme involves a chip-scale packaging (CSP) and materials development by its unit, Flexera Pte Ltd.</p>
<p>CSP is a packaging technology in which a semiconductor chip can be miniaturised.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
